{
  "teamId": 110,
  "year": 2024,
  "narrative": "The 2024 Baltimore Orioles opened the season with a burst of offensive energy that announced their intentions to the American League. Jordan Westburg emerged immediately as an unexpected catalyst, clubbing home runs in back-to-back series while veteran catcher James McCann delivered a clutch two-run single that set the early tone. The lineup looked deep, dangerous, and capable of carrying a club that had been building steadily through its rebuild years.\n\nThe middle chapters of the season, however, exposed a critical vulnerability: Craig Kimbrel. The veteran closer became the defining anxiety of the Baltimore summer, surrendering home runs and key hits at the worst possible moments throughout April, June, and July. His repeated late-inning collapses cost the Orioles wins they should have had, and the bullpen struggles extended to Keegan Akin, Gregory Soto, and Seranthony Domínguez as well. Every time the offense gave Baltimore a lead worth protecting, the relief corps found new and painful ways to give it back.\n\nThrough it all, Anthony Santander kept the Orioles afloat. He slugged his way to 44 home runs on the season, including a grand slam in August that felt like a declaration of individual brilliance even as the team around him wobbled. Cedric Mullins, Gunnar Henderson, Adley Rutschman, and a maturing Jackson Holliday all contributed momentum-swinging moments, and the club steadied itself down the stretch to finish 91-71 and secure a Wild Card berth. The offense, powered by 235 home runs, was never really the problem.\n\nOctober arrived with genuine hope, but the Wild Card round against Kansas City exposed the team's fragility in high-leverage moments. Corbin Burnes could only do so much, and Bobby Witt Jr. delivered a dagger single off Yennier Cano in Game 2 that ended Baltimore's season. The Orioles were eliminated in the Wild Card, a bitter conclusion to a season that showed both the enormous potential of this young core and the bullpen depth they would need to acquire if 2025 was going to end differently.",
